1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,604
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:28,862
[Helena] <i>I have a job for you.</i>

6
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:33,366
<i>Protect the diamonds</i>
<i>I've sent for the charity event.</i>

7
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,784
<i>Make sure that it gets there.</i>

8
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:37,203
[Raul] <i>Get ready because</i>
<i>we have another mission.</i>

9
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:39,122
<i>A certain package will arrive.</i>

10
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:42,333
<i>Diamonds worth 20 million.</i>
<i>We'll take them all.</i>

11
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:46,379
[Lily] <i>But we have to go there</i>
<i>so I can find out</i>

12
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:48,798
<i>who Helena Montoya really is.</i>

13
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:51,926
<i>That's when I'll find out</i>
<i>whether she's my enemy</i>

14
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:52,761
<i>or my ally.</i>

15
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:55,889
<i>You're here to seduce</i>
<i>my husband again, aren't you?</i>

16
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:58,516
<i>That's so last month. I've moved on.</i>

17
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:01,519
<i>Who could my new flavor of the month be?</i>

18
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,980
[Emilia] <i>Please escort this</i>
<i>little birdbrain out of here.</i>

19
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:07,400
-[Natalie] <i>I can walk!</i>
-[Emilia] <i>And do her a good job.</i>

20
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:09,277
[Damian] <i>Only an idiot</i>
<i>would betray Red Dragon.</i>

21
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:10,528
[man] <i>Someone's following us.</i>

22
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:11,446
[gunshots]

23
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:13,448
-[explosion]
-[Damian laughing]

24
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:16,659
<i>You better practice first,</i>
<i>if you want to get a punch in!</i>

25
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:18,036
[Natalie] <i>I already saved you before.</i>

26
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:20,955
<i>And thank you for saving me.</i>
<i>Now we're even.</i>

27
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,082
[Jepoy] <i>Just be careful.</i>

28
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:23,458
<i>I don't want this happening again.</i>

29
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:25,668
[Helena] <i>I would like to introduce to you</i>

30
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:30,298
<i>my long-lost daughter,</i>
<i>Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

31
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:34,677
[Lily] <i>Now I know why she</i>
<i>wants to get close to me.</i>

32
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:37,263
[Helena] <i>I only have good</i>
<i>intentions for this town.</i>

33
00:01:37,347 --> 00:01:41,142
<i>Why don't you join me and</i>
<i>my latest project for the town?</i>

34
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:43,436
<i>Sure, Helena. Sure.</i>

35
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:46,397
[Julio] <i>Those diamonds are only</i>
<i>beautiful to a fool</i>

36
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:47,899
<i>who thinks they don't come with a price.</i>

37
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:51,069
[Camia] <i>Be wary. You don't know</i>
<i>who you're up against.</i>

38
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:56,366
<i>They may have buried Ivy Aguas,</i>
<i>but her words still remain.</i>

39
00:01:56,449 --> 00:01:59,202
<i>So, to Emilia and Helena…</i>

40
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:00,829
<i>Don't try me.</i>

41
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:05,667
[tense music playing]

42
00:02:08,837 --> 00:02:10,880
We don't have an appointment, Helena.

43
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:12,423
I came here to surprise you.

44
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:14,884
You won't kick me out, will you?

45
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:16,386
I brought you something.

46
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:25,812
If it isn't the famous Lily Cruz.

47
00:02:25,895 --> 00:02:27,397
[Lily chuckles softly]

48
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,524
Why, of course

49
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,943
I'm going to welcome

50
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:35,488
a very sweet lady like you.

51
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:46,541
Oh… Helena, I have to say,

52
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:50,461
your causes have been so remarkable.

53
00:02:51,004 --> 00:02:52,672
That's why I decided to pay you a visit.

54
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:56,467
'Cause now I am your number one fan.

55
00:02:58,553 --> 00:03:03,641
I'm curious as to how
a high-profile jewelry designer,

56
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:06,853
artist, socially responsible humanitarian,

57
00:03:06,936 --> 00:03:09,856
became Emilia Ardiente's biological mother

58
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:13,359
and Julio Ardiente's ex-lover.

59
00:03:13,985 --> 00:03:17,572
No offense, Helena, but being involved

60
00:03:17,655 --> 00:03:20,950
with that family
is so outside your profile.

61
00:03:22,952 --> 00:03:24,787
It's really a long story, Lily.

62
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:30,084
I don't think you have the EQ
to listen to my life story.

63
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:32,128
No offense.

64
00:03:32,211 --> 00:03:37,008
[tense music playing]

65
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:54,692
Helena, try me. Try me.
I'll listen. Promise.

66
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:07,038
[birds chirping]

67
00:04:08,748 --> 00:04:09,791
Helena?

68
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:13,294
No. I don't know anyone named Helena.

69
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:17,382
Last night, during the event
at the capitol,

70
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:23,054
Helena Montoya introduced
herself as Emilia's mother.

71
00:04:23,137 --> 00:04:24,681
That makes her your grandmother.

72
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:27,350
Aren't you interested
in getting to know her?

73
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:33,106
Have you ever thought
of returning to your family?

74
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:34,899
Don't you think about them anymore?

75
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:39,487
I know why you're asking me this.

76
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:43,533
You're making sure I've really changed.

77
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:47,996
Do you still not trust me until now?

78
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,125
Thing is, Arnaldo,

79
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:56,212
you can't dictate what
people think about you.

80
00:04:57,547 --> 00:05:00,425
What's important
is you do good for others,

81
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:06,389
and one day, your actions
will prove who you really are.

82
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:09,767
[uplifting music playing]

83
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:18,234
[Camia] We need to tighten
the security at night.

84
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:19,193
-Yes, ma'am.
-Understood?

85
00:05:19,277 --> 00:05:21,946
-Yes, ma'am.
-All right. You may go.

86
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:24,949
[Damian] Camia.

87
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:28,202
Did Lily push through
with her meeting with Helena?

88
00:05:28,286 --> 00:05:29,579
Yes, Damian.

89
00:05:29,954 --> 00:05:34,208
But we both know that Lily won't
go to war unprepared.

90
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:38,171
[unsettling music playing]

91
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:41,299
Damian?

92
00:05:42,759 --> 00:05:43,968
Is there a problem?

93
00:05:45,136 --> 00:05:48,139
Do you know anything about
Helena Montoya that we don't?

94
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:50,224
[tense music playing]

95
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:52,226
Damian!

96
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:58,191
About Red Dragon, yes.

97
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:02,111
Red Dragon brought down Lily's business.

98
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:05,156
How is she connected to Helena Montoya?

99
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:12,038
Lily Cruz is Ivy Aguas.

100
00:06:13,247 --> 00:06:15,458
I know she'll get past all of this.

101
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:19,587
If she managed to fool
the Ardientes back then,

102
00:06:20,254 --> 00:06:23,299
then you're right,
we have nothing to worry about.

103
00:06:31,182 --> 00:06:34,519
I promised myself that after I gave birth,

104
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:38,064
my baby and I would escape
and live in peace.

105
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:40,191
-[doctor] <i>There's been a problem.</i>
-[Helena] <i>But it didn't happen.</i>

106
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:41,359
-[doctor] <i>But I promise…</i>
-<i>Where's my baby?!</i>

107
00:06:41,442 --> 00:06:42,777
<i>…we will do everything to save your baby.</i>

108
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,153
<i>Where are you taking my baby?!</i>

109
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:46,823
[Helena] <i>Julio made me believe</i>
<i>my baby was dead.</i>

110
00:06:47,448 --> 00:06:49,242
<i>And for so many years…</i>

111
00:06:49,325 --> 00:06:52,203
[Helena crying]

112
00:06:54,372 --> 00:06:58,584
For so many years,
I thought Emilia was dead.

113
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:04,090
But when I found out she was
alive, I searched for her.

114
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:08,052
And now, we're finally reunited.

115
00:07:08,719 --> 00:07:10,972
[sobs] I'm sorry. I just…

116
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:15,101
I get really passionate when
I talk about the people I love.

117
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:18,980
[exhales] How about you, Lily?

118
00:07:20,731 --> 00:07:24,068
I heard you and your mother
were separated too.

119
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:27,113
All because of the Ardientes.

120
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:34,203
That's not all, Helena.
The Ardientes killed my father.

121
00:07:35,746 --> 00:07:40,042
And they made my family's life hell.

122
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:44,881
And you staged an elaborate revenge plot.

123
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:48,509
Because it's only an eye for an eye.

124
00:07:48,593 --> 00:07:50,595
[tense music playing]

125
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:55,850
It's not my place to say this, but…

126
00:07:58,978 --> 00:08:00,897
I hope that you will forgive my family.

127
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:05,359
But if you loathe them, why are you here?

128
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:08,404
Am I now your enemy too?

129
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:13,242
Or is it because…
you're planning to use me?

130
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:17,997
Is that also why you haven't
declared war against me, Helena?

131
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:21,542
I'm not an Ardiente.

132
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:24,962
[chuckles] Tell you what, Lily--

133
00:08:25,671 --> 00:08:29,800
I enjoy talking to you. Why don't we…

134
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:33,846
see each other again?
Lunch or dinner, perhaps?

135
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:37,725
I thought you'd never ask, Helena.

136
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:40,394
[suspenseful music playing]

137
00:08:56,118 --> 00:08:57,203
So…

138
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:05,169
You finally convinced
your mother to fight Lily Cruz.

139
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:07,380
Why is that?

140
00:09:08,172 --> 00:09:12,760
Don't you find me a formidable
ally anymore,

141
00:09:12,843 --> 00:09:17,306
that you had to run to your
mother to find a new supporter?

142
00:09:19,016 --> 00:09:20,268
[sighs]

143
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:23,854
Papa, what are you upset about?
That I didn't approach you?

144
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:26,107
Or that I have a new ally in Mama?

145
00:09:28,526 --> 00:09:30,861
Don't be too presumptuous, my dear.

146
00:09:32,321 --> 00:09:36,951
Don't expect that your mother
can beat Lily Cruz.

147
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:41,914
Lily Cruz and your Mama
have a lot in common, you know.

148
00:09:42,832 --> 00:09:44,750
Maybe, in the end,

149
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:50,131
they might get along,
and you'll end up in the dust.

150
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:52,133
[both chuckle]

151
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:54,719
Well you can't poison
my mind anymore, Papa.

152
00:09:54,802 --> 00:09:58,681
In fact, I'm organizing
a reunion with my son and Mama.

153
00:09:59,056 --> 00:10:03,144
And you're not invited.
Who's left in the dust now, huh?

154
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:05,646
[chuckles mockingly]

155
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:06,731
Well…

156
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:08,899
Good luck…

157
00:10:10,359 --> 00:10:14,113
to your mini-reunion,

158
00:10:14,196 --> 00:10:15,781
good riddance,

159
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:20,202
and enjoy in the depths of Hades.

160
00:10:24,081 --> 00:10:25,791
Clan of devils.

161
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:29,378
-I lost my appetite.
-Good for you.

162
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:38,179
She asked for your forgiveness?
Helena Montoya?

163
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:44,602
Talk is cheap, Diego.
I don't get swayed by words.

164
00:10:44,977 --> 00:10:48,939
And her daughter is Emilia.
We really shouldn't trust her.

165
00:10:49,231 --> 00:10:50,941
But she let it all slide.

166
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:53,194
<i>She might not be an Ardiente,</i>

167
00:10:53,819 --> 00:10:58,991
but I'll find out every last
detail about Helena Montoya.

168
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:04,372
[suspenseful music playing]

169
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:10,961
[Arnaldo] Diego are you still
having trouble

170
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:12,213
with Helena Montoya?

171
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:17,385
Because Anna told me
that she's my grandmother.

172
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:18,469
Is that right?

173
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:21,347
We're concerned about anything
related to the Ardientes.

174
00:11:22,139 --> 00:11:24,016
Ah, okay.

175
00:11:25,142 --> 00:11:26,852
Then she's a bad person too.

176
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:30,564
I was just thinking…

177
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:33,192
do you still think I'm a bad person?

178
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:35,444
[pensive music playing]

179
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:40,991
[foreboding music playing]

180
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,878
What the hell are you doing here?!

181
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:55,172
Hey, Diego.

182
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:57,633
You think I don't know
that you want to take advantage

183
00:11:57,716 --> 00:12:00,886
of Arnaldo's sickness
for your own personal agenda?

184
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:04,348
-I'm not like you!
-Yeah, right! I know.

185
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:06,350
I know what you want to do, Diego.

186
00:12:06,434 --> 00:12:08,978
You want to take Arnaldo down
because he's sick right now.

187
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:12,565
But, I'll tell you,
he's going to rise again, okay?

188
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:16,861
Arnaldo, get away from him.
Okay, you. Toss out the garbage!

189
00:12:16,944 --> 00:12:19,155
Hold on a second! What are you doing?

190
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:21,198
Ouch!

191
00:12:21,407 --> 00:12:25,453
Stop it! I said, get Diego!
Why did you hurt Arnaldo?

192
00:12:25,536 --> 00:12:27,955
-He was in the way, ma'am.
-I was in the way?

193
00:12:28,038 --> 00:12:29,999
Enough, okay? This is enough.
You're going with me.

194
00:12:30,082 --> 00:12:32,084
[Arnaldo] I'm not going with you!

195
00:12:34,462 --> 00:12:37,298
The only thing that Diego did
was be a good brother to me.

196
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:40,301
You're coming with me
to meet your grandmother.

197
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:45,890
You… This isn't over.

198
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:47,975
Let's go!

199
00:12:50,352 --> 00:12:52,897
Open the door! Hurry!

200
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,692
[car doors closing]

201
00:12:57,026 --> 00:12:58,152
[car engine turns over]

202
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:11,540
That Diego Torillo has
always been a nuisance

203
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:13,584
to the Ardiente family, Mama.

204
00:13:15,252 --> 00:13:17,338
Why haven't you had him killed yet?

205
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:21,717
If you had, you wouldn't
be having this problem.

206
00:13:22,593 --> 00:13:25,221
You know, Mama, you're right.
But it's never too late.

207
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:28,724
I want Diego Torillo's head.

208
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:33,521
Oh, I have the perfect man for that.
The formidable Jaguar.

209
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:37,650
Jaguar? You know him, Mama?

210
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,235
[Emilia scoffs]

211
00:13:39,318 --> 00:13:42,738
What a small world,
and lots of coincidence, Mama.

212
00:13:42,821 --> 00:13:44,323
I know him too.

213
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:46,742
-Really?
-Yes, Mama.

214
00:13:46,825 --> 00:13:48,410
I know him very well.

215
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:51,372
[dramatic music playing]

216
00:13:57,336 --> 00:13:59,171
-Here.
-Oh. Thanks.

217
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:04,969
Are you okay?

218
00:14:06,762 --> 00:14:09,306
I'm fine. This is nothing.

219
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:12,768
[exhales]

220
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:14,853
Are you sure about what you did earlier?

221
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:22,236
Did I do something wrong?

222
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:24,446
I just did what I thought was right.

223
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:30,452
You don't plan on meeting
your grandmother?

224
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:35,165
Come to think of it, I do.

225
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:40,504
I want to meet her, but it's a mess there.

226
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:43,299
Yes, they're rich, but they're miserable.

227
00:14:44,466 --> 00:14:46,260
I'd rather stay here.

228
00:14:47,261 --> 00:14:50,014
It's really quiet here, but I'm happy.

229
00:14:53,684 --> 00:14:56,437
That's why I was hoping you'd tell them

230
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,480
that I just want to stay here.

231
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:01,692
[uplifting music playing]

232
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,361
[exhales]

233
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:12,328
Oh! Jaguar, darling!

234
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:16,624
This is your next bull's-eye.

235
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:19,168
Diego Torillo.

236
00:15:20,127 --> 00:15:22,254
Special request of my daughter.

237
00:15:23,881 --> 00:15:25,382
Isn't she lovely?

238
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:28,385
Um…

239
00:15:29,553 --> 00:15:35,684
So, Jaguar, when do we discuss
Diego Torillo's murder?

240
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:38,437
Just call me when you want the job done.

241
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:49,490
[laughs] Mama! Whee! I'm so happy!

242
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:52,368
[sighs] Let's drink to that.

243
00:15:55,079 --> 00:15:55,871
[glasses clink]

244
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:02,795
I can't do this. I won't do this!

245
00:16:02,878 --> 00:16:06,048
[action music playing]

246
00:16:06,757 --> 00:16:09,802
[Helena] <i>This is your next bull's-eye.</i>

247
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:11,303
<i>Diego Torillo.</i>

248
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:13,722
<i>Special request of my daughter.</i>

249
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:15,224
<i>Pay attention.</i>

250
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:18,978
<i>That's what I want to do</i>
<i>to my new enemies.</i>

251
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:22,523
<i>Because fire melts gold.</i>

252
00:16:23,732 --> 00:16:26,527
<i>I want to burn Lily Cruz alive!</i>

253
00:16:27,236 --> 00:16:29,947
[tense music playing]

254
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:48,048
-[grunts]
-[phone clatters]

255
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:49,883
[tense music playing]

256
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:52,553
Damian.

257
00:16:55,681 --> 00:16:57,016
What's going on?

258
00:17:03,105 --> 00:17:06,442
Why do you have this? Answer me, Damian!

259
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:09,737
Where is Lily?

260
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:24,043
<i>But if you loathe them, why are you here?</i>

261
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:26,587
<i>Am I now your enemy too?</i>

262
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:30,174
<i>Or is it because</i>
<i>you're planning to use me?</i>

263
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:35,137
<i>Is that also why you haven't</i>
<i>declared war against me, Helena?</i>

264
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:38,515
<i>I'm not an Ardiente. Tell you what, Lily--</i>

265
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:41,143
<i>I enjoy talking to you. Why don't we…</i>

266
00:17:41,226 --> 00:17:44,063
<i>see each other again?</i>
<i>Lunch or dinner, perhaps?</i>

267
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:52,946
<i>I've already played this game</i>
<i>before, Helena.</i>

268
00:17:53,822 --> 00:17:56,533
<i>So, hold on to your head.</i>

269
00:17:57,034 --> 00:18:01,663
<i>Because I'm going to uncover</i>
<i>every secret you've got.</i>

270
00:18:23,977 --> 00:18:25,270
I will charm you…

271
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:29,149
and trap you like a moth to a flame.

272
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:34,279
I will be the sweetest, most glamorous,

273
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:37,491
fabulous mother you never had, Lily Cruz.

274
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:40,702
And once you've grown so attached to me…

275
00:18:42,037 --> 00:18:44,164
that's when I'll swallow
you whole! [hisses]

276
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:46,959
[laughs]

277
00:18:47,376 --> 00:18:49,169
[foreboding music playing]

278
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:52,131
[phone rings]

279
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:55,008
Mercedes.

280
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:58,679
Madam, I can't contact Jaguar.

281
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:03,851
You can't contact Jaguar?

282
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:08,272
Idiot! You act like
you're not my underling!

283
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:14,736
You know what to do.
So, stop wasting my time.

284
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:28,000
[foreboding music continues]

285
00:19:38,969 --> 00:19:40,137
Don't worry, Mom.

286
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:43,599
I'll let you know once
I've met up with Helena.

287
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:46,351
-As always, be careful.
-I will.

288
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:49,813
I'll be leaving now.

289
00:19:51,315 --> 00:19:52,316
Lily.

290
00:19:54,276 --> 00:19:55,277
Yes, Uncle?

291
00:20:03,118 --> 00:20:06,788
Lily, you're facing
a very unpredictable enemy.

292
00:20:08,081 --> 00:20:11,668
So, listen to me. Red Dragon is…

293
00:20:11,752 --> 00:20:13,754
[suspenseful music swelling]

294
00:20:15,297 --> 00:20:17,549
[tense music]

295
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:19,635
[eerie music]

296
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:25,098
Hurry. You should leave.

297
00:20:25,682 --> 00:20:26,892
Be careful out there.

298
00:20:28,185 --> 00:20:29,228
Take care.

299
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:32,397
[tense music playing]

300
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:36,151
[car door closes]

301
00:20:37,444 --> 00:20:39,363
[tense music playing]

302
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:40,781
Camia, go on inside.

303
00:20:41,823 --> 00:20:42,783
[car door closes]

304
00:20:42,866 --> 00:20:44,159
[tense music playing]

305
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:45,285
[car engine turns over]

306
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:48,455
[tense music continues]

307
00:21:04,888 --> 00:21:09,893
[suspenseful music playing]

308
00:21:15,816 --> 00:21:16,817
[exhales deeply]

309
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:18,610
What are you doing here?

310
00:21:19,611 --> 00:21:21,571
I'm glad you got the message quickly.

311
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:25,575
But the next time you decide to
cut off communication with us,

312
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:28,787
you better make sure I don't find you.

313
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:30,956
[suspenseful music]

314
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:34,751
[Mercedes] This is for you.

315
00:21:45,262 --> 00:21:49,099
And this is the gun
I'll be using on Camia and Lily

316
00:21:49,182 --> 00:21:52,978
the moment you defy Red Dragon's orders.

317
00:21:53,812 --> 00:21:56,982
[tense music playing]

318
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:06,533
[Lily and Helena chuckling]

319
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:09,369
This is the best dim sum in the metro.

320
00:22:10,454 --> 00:22:13,957
So, I guess you really
enjoy Chinese cuisine?

321
00:22:15,125 --> 00:22:18,378
From time to time.
But, you know what, Lily?

322
00:22:18,462 --> 00:22:20,547
I'm very happy that you're here today.

323
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,467
-My day's been made.
-[Lily chuckles]

324
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:27,220
But more so, if you accepted my proposal.

325
00:22:30,098 --> 00:22:35,604
I'm organizing…
a women empowerment seminar.

326
00:22:35,979 --> 00:22:38,023
And I want us to work together.

327
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:40,484
I want you to be the guest speaker.

328
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:41,943
What do you say?

329
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:44,404
Sure, Helena.

330
00:22:44,821 --> 00:22:46,907
After all, I'm the type of woman
who never backs down

331
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:49,785
from a fight or lets anyone get in my way.

332
00:22:51,078 --> 00:22:52,537
I am Lily Cruz.

333
00:22:52,621 --> 00:22:56,458
And, like I told the Ardientes,
I am indestructible.

334
00:22:56,541 --> 00:22:58,543
[both laugh]

335
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:00,420
Well, that makes the two of us.

336
00:23:01,421 --> 00:23:05,717
We have so much in common.
We could be best friends!

337
00:23:08,553 --> 00:23:09,429
To friendship.

338
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:13,016
To friendship.

339
00:23:14,476 --> 00:23:15,685
[glasses clink]

340
00:23:16,019 --> 00:23:18,939
[tense music playing]

341
00:23:46,591 --> 00:23:49,511
-Where are you going, Damian?
-Don't mind me, Camia.

342
00:23:50,595 --> 00:23:51,763
Damian, wait!

343
00:23:52,556 --> 00:23:54,933
Where are you going? Manila? Work?

344
00:23:55,016 --> 00:23:57,477
I know there's something
you're not telling me!

345
00:23:58,019 --> 00:24:00,897
I won't let you leave
until you tell me the truth!

346
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:03,483
I don't have to tell you anything.

347
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:07,028
What is it you were about to
tell Lily about Red Dragon?

348
00:24:07,821 --> 00:24:09,906
Do you know anything about Red Dragon?

349
00:24:11,032 --> 00:24:12,325
Answer me, Damian!

350
00:24:13,326 --> 00:24:16,079
Are you part of Red Dragon's syndicate?

351
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:26,256
[line ringing]

352
00:24:26,798 --> 00:24:28,049
Hello, Jaguar.

353
00:24:29,134 --> 00:24:30,969
I thought you were avoiding me.

354
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:32,804
You were so cold earlier.

355
00:24:32,888 --> 00:24:33,972
[scoffs]

356
00:24:34,431 --> 00:24:36,183
What are you talking about, Emilia?

357
00:24:36,766 --> 00:24:39,936
Because when Red Dragon and I
asked you to kill Diego Torillo,

358
00:24:40,729 --> 00:24:43,398
<i>you just said a few words and left.</i>

359
00:24:44,232 --> 00:24:46,610
Oh, about what happened…

360
00:24:46,943 --> 00:24:50,071
Sorry about that. I was just tired.

361
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,616
So, when do you want me to do it?

362
00:24:53,408 --> 00:24:56,244
Anyway, do it at your own
pace and leisure.

363
00:24:56,745 --> 00:25:00,665
But I'd just like to remind you,
I don't like waiting too long.

364
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:02,959
You can count on me, Emilia.

365
00:25:03,835 --> 00:25:07,839
I'll give you Diego Torillo's head
on a silver platter.

366
00:25:08,715 --> 00:25:10,634
You are so awesome!

367
00:25:21,853 --> 00:25:22,896
No.

368
00:25:25,607 --> 00:25:27,317
But I know of Red Dragon.

369
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,946
Her name was everywhere
when I was still a criminal.

370
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:34,908
Because those who stood in
her way were killed mercilessly.

371
00:25:36,326 --> 00:25:37,827
That's why I asked Lily

372
00:25:37,911 --> 00:25:40,997
to stop messing with her
before it's too late.

373
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:46,294
I can't let anything bad happen to her…

374
00:25:50,257 --> 00:25:52,133
and especially not to you, Camia.

375
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:57,264
[dramatic music playing]

376
00:26:34,050 --> 00:26:35,302
[phone ringing]

377
00:26:40,223 --> 00:26:42,475
-Go on.
-[ringing continues]

378
00:26:44,602 --> 00:26:46,396
-Dad?
-[Raul] <i>Hello, Diego.</i>

379
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:49,065
Listen closely, son.

380
00:26:49,858 --> 00:26:51,109
You need to hide.

381
00:26:51,860 --> 00:26:54,070
Because you're Red Dragon's next target.

382
00:26:55,530 --> 00:26:58,366
What? How did you find out?

383
00:26:59,117 --> 00:27:01,411
<i>Who's Red Dragon? Do you know her?</i>

384
00:27:02,746 --> 00:27:04,831
[Raul] <i>I'll explain everything</i>
<i>in due time.</i>

385
00:27:04,914 --> 00:27:06,541
<i>But for now, you have to watch your back.</i>

386
00:27:06,916 --> 00:27:09,711
Thanks, Dad. But I'm not afraid of her.

387
00:27:10,628 --> 00:27:14,215
And we'll do everything
to bring Red Dragon down.

388
00:27:14,924 --> 00:27:16,009
Diego, wait--

389
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:18,053
Diego?!

390
00:27:18,136 --> 00:27:21,431
[tense music playing]

391
00:27:25,310 --> 00:27:26,269
[sighs]

392
00:27:27,062 --> 00:27:28,938
<i>If you won't listen to me,</i>

393
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:32,108
<i>then I'll protect you the way I know how.</i>

394
00:27:37,238 --> 00:27:40,325
Well… I'm so happy that you're on board.

395
00:27:40,909 --> 00:27:43,787
And I'm thankful that,
despite your differences

396
00:27:43,870 --> 00:27:46,122
with my daughter, we can still be friends.

397
00:27:46,664 --> 00:27:47,665
Oh.

398
00:27:51,669 --> 00:27:54,339
-Here's my card.
-Oh. Thank you.

399
00:27:57,133 --> 00:27:58,301
Here's mine.

400
00:28:00,845 --> 00:28:01,846
All right.

401
00:28:03,431 --> 00:28:04,808
[exhales] Helena.

402
00:28:06,810 --> 00:28:09,979
I didn't think I'd be
this comfortable around you.

403
00:28:11,189 --> 00:28:13,983
You're like the glamorous mother
that I never had.

404
00:28:14,818 --> 00:28:17,112
-So… bye.
-Bye.

405
00:28:32,752 --> 00:28:37,006
Say goodbye to the world soon, Lily Cruz.

406
00:28:37,090 --> 00:28:39,134
[eerie music]

407
00:28:43,972 --> 00:28:45,014
Hello, Madam?

408
00:28:48,226 --> 00:28:49,185
[Helena] <i>Mercedes…</i>

409
00:28:49,269 --> 00:28:52,731
-Meet me at the VIP room.
-Right away.

410
00:28:52,814 --> 00:28:54,816
[suspenseful music playing]

411
00:28:57,736 --> 00:29:01,573
<i>Madam? Who were you talking to?</i>

412
00:29:24,804 --> 00:29:31,436
<i>Are you working for my enemy?</i>
<i>Are you Mercedes Palacio?</i>

413
00:29:31,519 --> 00:29:34,731
[suspenseful music continues]

414
00:29:37,776 --> 00:29:39,611
Um… It's okay!

415
00:29:39,694 --> 00:29:42,489
You can have this table. I'm done, anyway.

416
00:29:44,741 --> 00:29:45,825
[Mercedes] Thank you.

417
00:29:51,247 --> 00:29:52,457
-Miss.
-Yes?

418
00:29:52,540 --> 00:29:55,376
Next time, don't mix up
the reservations, okay?

419
00:29:55,460 --> 00:29:57,420
Uh, okay, ma'am. I'm really sorry.

420
00:29:59,047 --> 00:30:02,675
[suspenseful music continues]

421
00:30:31,329 --> 00:30:34,582
[somber piano music playing]

422
00:30:37,544 --> 00:30:39,712
<i>You're staying with me.</i>
<i>You're my little puppy dog!</i>

423
00:30:39,796 --> 00:30:40,964
<i>What?</i>

424
00:30:42,340 --> 00:30:43,716
<i>I'm not your little pet!</i>

425
00:30:43,967 --> 00:30:45,343
<i>So, don't strangle me!</i>

426
00:30:45,426 --> 00:30:47,470
<i>Use me all you want, but remember this…</i>

427
00:30:48,972 --> 00:30:50,265
<i>You can't control me.</i>

428
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:56,896
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

429
00:30:56,980 --> 00:30:58,565
<i>Please try again later.</i>

430
00:31:05,947 --> 00:31:06,823
-<i>The subscriber…</i>
-Ah!

431
00:31:06,906 --> 00:31:07,866
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

432
00:31:07,949 --> 00:31:09,325
<i>Please try again later.</i>

433
00:31:11,327 --> 00:31:12,328
[grunts]

434
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:17,333
How dare you, Madrigal!

435
00:31:18,626 --> 00:31:21,337
<i>Why would you even come back to me</i>

436
00:31:21,421 --> 00:31:23,798
<i>when I said for you to leave me alone?</i>

437
00:31:24,507 --> 00:31:28,386
I told you… to leave me alone.

438
00:31:28,469 --> 00:31:31,848
And that's when you actually made a move.

439
00:31:32,432 --> 00:31:34,225
[chuckles] <i>Why?</i>

440
00:31:35,059 --> 00:31:38,396
<i>Why would you kiss me…</i>
<i>and leave me hanging?</i>

441
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:42,233
[scoffs] I hate you.

442
00:31:43,109 --> 00:31:46,112
I hate you so much!

443
00:31:50,158 --> 00:31:51,951
What's wrong with you, Natalie?

444
00:31:53,244 --> 00:31:58,458
[chuckles] Can you still
do this? Natalie? Hello?

445
00:32:00,126 --> 00:32:03,671
He is Madrigal.

446
00:32:04,714 --> 00:32:09,010
[chuckles] <i>Ew! Why are you so worked up?</i>

447
00:32:12,388 --> 00:32:15,266
Do you actually have feelings
for Madrigal?

448
00:32:16,809 --> 00:32:23,483
[laughs] No…
You have feelings for Madrigal!

449
00:32:26,694 --> 00:32:31,157
Ew! Ew! No.

450
00:32:32,659 --> 00:32:35,954
Madrigal won't fall in love with you.

451
00:32:36,663 --> 00:32:39,666
<i>And he will never love you</i>
<i>the way he loves</i>

452
00:32:39,749 --> 00:32:41,584
Lily Cruz.

453
00:32:42,835 --> 00:32:43,920
Get it?

454
00:32:44,963 --> 00:32:46,089
[chuckles]

455
00:32:48,424 --> 00:32:49,592
Or can he?

456
00:32:52,345 --> 00:32:56,891
Can Madrigal fall in love with me?

457
00:33:04,399 --> 00:33:06,234
Could he actually love me?

458
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:11,155
How?

459
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:19,288
<i>Ivy Aguas? Or is it Lily Cruz?</i>

460
00:33:23,292 --> 00:33:26,379
Through Lily.

461
00:33:28,172 --> 00:33:29,173
Through Lily!

462
00:33:29,549 --> 00:33:31,634
[laughs]

463
00:33:33,219 --> 00:33:34,220
[exhales]

464
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:43,021
[comical music]

465
00:33:43,104 --> 00:33:44,856
[Arnaldo exhales] Uh--

466
00:33:44,939 --> 00:33:47,400
You make it look so easy, but it's hard.

467
00:33:47,483 --> 00:33:50,862
Uh… But thanks for helping me out.

468
00:33:51,821 --> 00:33:54,032
I appreciate that you're checking on me.

469
00:33:54,115 --> 00:33:55,158
Thank you so much.

470
00:33:56,951 --> 00:33:58,369
You're really kind, Diego.

471
00:33:58,953 --> 00:34:00,788
I must say, I'm a bit embarrassed because…

472
00:34:01,164 --> 00:34:05,043
it's like you're
the older brother between us.

473
00:34:05,126 --> 00:34:07,712
Tell me, I was the mature one
when we were kids, right?

474
00:34:09,714 --> 00:34:12,884
[soft piano music playing]

475
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:21,768
<i>Swallow it.</i>

476
00:34:24,437 --> 00:34:27,106
<i>Stop that. You sound like a dying pig.</i>

477
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:30,860
<i>If Grandpa hears you crying,</i>
<i>he'll serve you for dinner.</i>

478
00:34:30,943 --> 00:34:32,236
-[Diego continues crying]
-<i>You baby pig.</i>

479
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:36,532
[Emilia] <i>Starting tomorrow, I'm</i>
<i>gonna put you on a diet.</i>

480
00:34:36,616 --> 00:34:40,078
<i>He's always full!</i>
<i>He only needs one tummy rub</i>

481
00:34:40,161 --> 00:34:42,371
<i>before he falls asleep like a pig!</i>

482
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:43,498
<i>It's true.</i>

483
00:34:46,959 --> 00:34:48,002
Yeah.

484
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:56,219
In that case, I really need to learn this.

485
00:35:06,854 --> 00:35:09,273
[ring clattering]

486
00:35:09,357 --> 00:35:13,194
[bittersweet music playing]

487
00:35:14,403 --> 00:35:15,822
[young Julio]
<i>I have something else for you.</i>

488
00:35:17,156 --> 00:35:20,034
<i>It's a promise ring. Helena, I love you.</i>

489
00:35:21,536 --> 00:35:24,831
<i>I promise to marry you</i>
<i>and be with you forever.</i>

490
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:29,961
<i>Once I achieve my dream</i>
<i>of becoming president,</i>

491
00:35:30,044 --> 00:35:31,587
<i>you'll be my first lady.</i>

492
00:35:31,671 --> 00:35:34,966
<i>Of course, Julio. I love you.</i>

493
00:35:35,258 --> 00:35:36,551
<i>I love you too, Helena.</i>

494
00:35:37,009 --> 00:35:40,805
[music continues]

495
00:35:45,226 --> 00:35:48,437
<i>-Julio, wait.</i>
<i>-You whore! You cheated on me!</i>

496
00:35:50,606 --> 00:35:52,525
Damn you, Helena.

497
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:57,613
You give women all over
the world a bad name.

498
00:35:59,407 --> 00:36:02,827
No matter how you might explain it…

499
00:36:04,245 --> 00:36:06,164
you still deceived me.

500
00:36:06,706 --> 00:36:08,374
[dramatic music]

501
00:36:08,457 --> 00:36:11,919
You're no different from Esmeralda.

502
00:36:14,130 --> 00:36:18,050
You chose a worthless man over me.

503
00:36:19,093 --> 00:36:23,347
Emilia's misery isn't enough

504
00:36:24,390 --> 00:36:27,476
to pay for all the pain
and humiliation you gave me.

505
00:36:28,686 --> 00:36:31,522
That is why I swore to myself

506
00:36:33,024 --> 00:36:36,194
that I'd make you crawl in the mud

507
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:38,487
the moment you returned to Ardiente.

508
00:36:38,571 --> 00:36:42,241
[dramatic music intensifies]

509
00:36:53,002 --> 00:36:57,632
Damn you, Helena! I still love you.

510
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:03,221
[sniffles]

511
00:37:03,471 --> 00:37:04,472
[exhales]

512
00:37:10,311 --> 00:37:11,979
[breathes deeply]

513
00:37:16,442 --> 00:37:19,070
Didn't you push me away the other day?

514
00:37:21,113 --> 00:37:22,240
I knew it.

515
00:37:24,992 --> 00:37:26,160
You like me.

516
00:37:27,703 --> 00:37:28,788
No.

517
00:37:29,830 --> 00:37:31,666
I would never blur the lines

518
00:37:31,749 --> 00:37:34,669
between someone I'm just sleeping with.

519
00:37:36,128 --> 00:37:41,008
Besides, I know exactly what
kind of relationship we have.

520
00:37:41,968 --> 00:37:43,552
Then why'd you ask me to come here?

521
00:37:44,553 --> 00:37:46,722
Because I want to make a proposal.

522
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:51,727
I want to help Lily.

523
00:37:53,729 --> 00:37:55,273
In her fight against the Ardientes.

524
00:37:55,898 --> 00:37:57,566
I've made up my mind.

525
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:01,153
Lily doesn't need your help.

526
00:38:02,154 --> 00:38:03,155
Maybe.

527
00:38:03,864 --> 00:38:04,991
For now.

528
00:38:05,908 --> 00:38:08,619
It's gonna be a tactical alliance.

529
00:38:09,453 --> 00:38:14,667
And it should've been like that
a long time ago

530
00:38:14,750 --> 00:38:16,711
since we have the same enemies.

531
00:38:18,212 --> 00:38:19,213
Really?

532
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:25,011
All right. Tell me.

533
00:38:29,348 --> 00:38:31,058
What made you change your mind?

534
00:38:34,061 --> 00:38:35,187
Well…

535
00:38:35,938 --> 00:38:38,649
I've decided that I want to place my bets

536
00:38:38,733 --> 00:38:43,237
and my resources on the winning team.

537
00:38:45,990 --> 00:38:47,450
And I think…

538
00:38:49,243 --> 00:38:51,412
Lily's in the right.

539
00:38:54,123 --> 00:38:56,751
And I want to fight for what's right.

540
00:39:01,630 --> 00:39:02,757
Are you sure?

541
00:39:04,216 --> 00:39:05,009
Mm-hm.

542
00:39:05,092 --> 00:39:10,097
[bleak string music playing]

543
00:39:14,852 --> 00:39:17,021
All right. If you say so.

544
00:39:25,905 --> 00:39:26,989
[Natalie chuckles]

545
00:39:44,340 --> 00:39:46,175
Lily, are you sure

546
00:39:46,258 --> 00:39:49,720
you saw Helena Montoya
with Mercedes Palacio?

547
00:39:52,056 --> 00:39:53,641
Well, I can't be too sure.

548
00:39:54,308 --> 00:39:59,230
But something tells me that Helena Montoya

549
00:39:59,313 --> 00:40:02,691
is somehow connected to Mercedes Palacio.

550
00:40:06,404 --> 00:40:07,405
[phone ringing]

551
00:40:10,241 --> 00:40:11,784
Speak of the devil.

552
00:40:15,663 --> 00:40:17,706
-Helena!
-Lily!

553
00:40:18,457 --> 00:40:21,210
I called to say
how much I enjoyed our lunch.

554
00:40:21,544 --> 00:40:25,172
Mmm… Me too. I feel the same way.

555
00:40:26,507 --> 00:40:28,384
[Helena] <i>So, when is our next lunch date?</i>

556
00:40:29,343 --> 00:40:32,054
That way, we can talk about our project.

557
00:40:32,471 --> 00:40:33,597
[chuckles]

558
00:40:34,432 --> 00:40:35,975
Well, my schedule's a little tight.

559
00:40:36,434 --> 00:40:39,895
But don't worry, my
people will call your people.

560
00:40:40,438 --> 00:40:43,065
<i>I can't wait to see you again, my friend.</i>

561
00:40:43,149 --> 00:40:44,024
Bye.

562
00:40:44,442 --> 00:40:48,988
[suspenseful music swelling]

563
00:40:54,785 --> 00:40:55,786
Mercedes.

564
00:41:00,207 --> 00:41:02,334
It's either Lily didn't see us,

565
00:41:02,418 --> 00:41:05,212
or she's just pretending she
doesn't know we're connected.

566
00:41:06,380 --> 00:41:08,340
Either way, we have to be careful.

567
00:41:09,133 --> 00:41:12,344
She can't find out
that we know each other.

568
00:41:12,428 --> 00:41:15,097
[tense music playing]

569
00:41:22,104 --> 00:41:24,815
[Jenny] Here are the roses we
picked from the garden, ma'am.

570
00:41:24,899 --> 00:41:27,026
All right. Wait. Is the food ready?

571
00:41:27,109 --> 00:41:29,028
Yes, ma'am. The chef's preparing it.

572
00:41:29,111 --> 00:41:31,238
Very good. Okay.

573
00:41:32,698 --> 00:41:35,284
Well, well, well…

574
00:41:36,410 --> 00:41:40,206
If there's one thing you really
got from your mother…

575
00:41:40,873 --> 00:41:43,959
it's how excited you get

576
00:41:44,043 --> 00:41:46,587
whenever there's a party being thrown.

577
00:41:47,004 --> 00:41:50,174
You can't flatter your way
to get an invitation, Papa.

578
00:41:50,633 --> 00:41:52,801
Oh, I don't need an invitation.

579
00:41:54,178 --> 00:41:56,263
All I have to do is show up!

580
00:41:57,348 --> 00:42:00,976
Or have you forgotten…
that this is my house?

581
00:42:02,353 --> 00:42:03,395
Besides…

582
00:42:04,313 --> 00:42:09,276
how can there even be a reunion
when my grandson isn't here?

583
00:42:09,985 --> 00:42:13,322
Don't worry, Papa. He's on his way here.

584
00:42:14,740 --> 00:42:17,284
-This flower isn't any good…
-We'll see.

585
00:42:18,244 --> 00:42:20,454
Oh, no. Let's change this. Okay.

586
00:42:20,538 --> 00:42:24,375
-[Julio scoffs]
-[Emilia humming]

587
00:42:28,629 --> 00:42:31,966
If you need anything… just let me know.

588
00:42:32,508 --> 00:42:33,425
Thanks.

589
00:42:33,509 --> 00:42:35,970
[suspenseful music playing]

590
00:42:40,891 --> 00:42:42,768
-What do you want?
-We're taking Arnaldo back home!

591
00:42:42,851 --> 00:42:44,645
Stay out of this!

592
00:42:44,728 --> 00:42:46,855
Didn't I say I wasn't going with you?

593
00:42:46,939 --> 00:42:49,275
You don't have a choice anymore.

594
00:42:49,358 --> 00:42:50,359
Now, come with us.

595
00:42:50,442 --> 00:42:52,945
-Wait!
-Let me go! Let me go!

596
00:42:53,028 --> 00:42:55,155
-Wait!
-[grunts] Let me go! Let me go!

597
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:56,282
-Take him!
-Diego!

598
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:00,911
-[bodyguard grunts]
-Diego!

599
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:02,204
[Arnaldo grunts]

600
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:06,875
[Arnaldo grunting] Let go of me!

601
00:43:06,959 --> 00:43:07,960
[groans]

602
00:43:08,919 --> 00:43:11,338
[grunting]

603
00:43:11,422 --> 00:43:12,923
[Arnaldo groaning]

604
00:43:14,049 --> 00:43:15,092
Watch out! [grunts]

605
00:43:19,972 --> 00:43:20,973
[screams]

606
00:43:24,393 --> 00:43:25,352
[bodyguard grunts]

607
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:35,446
[bodyguard groans]

608
00:43:39,408 --> 00:43:41,243
Go on! Try me!

609
00:43:42,161 --> 00:43:43,287
Leave now while you can!

610
00:43:44,246 --> 00:43:45,581
-[bodyguard groans]
-Leave!

611
00:43:46,957 --> 00:43:47,958
Arnaldo.

612
00:43:50,336 --> 00:43:51,337
[car engine turns over]

613
00:43:53,297 --> 00:43:54,882
[panting]

614
00:43:56,258 --> 00:43:59,595
[tense music playing]

615
00:44:03,766 --> 00:44:04,600
Are you all right?

616
00:44:04,683 --> 00:44:07,936
[panting] Yes. How about you?

617
00:44:11,190 --> 00:44:12,775
[panting]

618
00:44:13,108 --> 00:44:14,151
Thanks.

619
00:44:20,783 --> 00:44:23,077
It's about time. You're late.

620
00:44:23,619 --> 00:44:26,246
I don't think you're invited
to the occasion.

621
00:44:26,330 --> 00:44:29,875
[laughs] This is my house.

622
00:44:29,958 --> 00:44:33,045
And whether you like it or not,
we're still family.

623
00:44:33,128 --> 00:44:34,254
[scoffs]

624
00:44:34,338 --> 00:44:39,218
Poor little Julio. Still hoping
we'll get back together.

625
00:44:41,053 --> 00:44:44,348
-I never said that.
-You were my husband.

626
00:44:45,265 --> 00:44:47,393
I know you inside and out.

627
00:44:47,476 --> 00:44:53,148
I have no doubt in my heart.
I know that you still love me.

628
00:44:53,524 --> 00:44:57,444
[laughs] Come on, Helena.

629
00:44:59,613 --> 00:45:04,076
If I kiss you right now,
would you stop me?

630
00:45:04,993 --> 00:45:07,454
[dramatic music]

631
00:45:08,914 --> 00:45:10,791
[laughs] Got you!

632
00:45:12,334 --> 00:45:15,546
[Helena laughing]

633
00:45:22,803 --> 00:45:24,179
This is not funny.

634
00:45:33,856 --> 00:45:36,275
[suspenseful music swelling]

635
00:45:38,235 --> 00:45:39,403
<i>Hello, Madam?</i>

636
00:46:16,106 --> 00:46:19,109
<i>I'll find you, Mercedes Palacio.</i>

637
00:46:19,193 --> 00:46:24,448
<i>And I'll know your connection</i>
<i>to Helena Montoya.</i>

638
00:46:31,455 --> 00:46:35,417
I'm sorry, ma'am,
but they ganged up on us.

639
00:46:35,501 --> 00:46:37,711
He didn't let us take Diego Torillo.

640
00:46:39,338 --> 00:46:41,673
-What do I even pay you for?!
-My goodness.

641
00:46:41,757 --> 00:46:43,050
-You idiot!
-Emilia, darling.

642
00:46:43,133 --> 00:46:44,468
Emilia. Come on. Calm down.

643
00:46:44,551 --> 00:46:46,887
It's okay, baby. It's okay.

644
00:46:46,970 --> 00:46:47,971
[Emilia sighs]

645
00:46:49,181 --> 00:46:50,224
Are you okay?

646
00:46:51,058 --> 00:46:52,976
It's okay. You can go, darling.

647
00:46:56,772 --> 00:46:58,899
I'm sorry for wasting your time, Mama.

648
00:46:58,982 --> 00:47:01,109
Oh, it's okay, my dear.

649
00:47:01,193 --> 00:47:03,820
I can always meet my grandson
some other time.

650
00:47:10,160 --> 00:47:13,038
But I hope nothing comes between
me and Arnaldo next time.

651
00:47:15,165 --> 00:47:20,212
And you're right, Emilia.
Diego is a thorn.

652
00:47:22,589 --> 00:47:25,217
So, if you don't do something
about it tonight…

653
00:47:26,760 --> 00:47:30,180
then you are the biggest thorn
in this family!

654
00:47:30,264 --> 00:47:33,267
[tense music playing]

655
00:47:45,112 --> 00:47:48,699
Damian, is there really
no stopping you from leaving?

656
00:47:53,537 --> 00:47:57,082
Damian, we're your family.

657
00:47:57,165 --> 00:48:00,252
No matter what problems you have,
we can face them together.

658
00:48:00,752 --> 00:48:05,382
We can trust Lily to handle herself
against Red Dragon.

659
00:48:06,008 --> 00:48:07,551
And if you stay here,

660
00:48:07,634 --> 00:48:11,221
you can protect Lily,
and Lily can protect you,

661
00:48:11,305 --> 00:48:14,224
especially since you've already left
Red Dragon's syndicate.

662
00:48:18,937 --> 00:48:21,940
Damian, don't forget we all love you.

663
00:48:23,358 --> 00:48:25,444
Whatever it is you're going through,

664
00:48:25,527 --> 00:48:28,071
remember that we're ready
to fight with you,

665
00:48:28,155 --> 00:48:29,531
as long as you stay true to us.

666
00:48:29,615 --> 00:48:32,909
[tense music playing]

667
00:48:37,456 --> 00:48:38,790
[phone rings]

668
00:48:44,171 --> 00:48:44,963
Hello?

669
00:48:45,047 --> 00:48:48,216
Weren't you tasked to get
Diego Torillo's head?

670
00:48:48,550 --> 00:48:49,760
Have you started?

671
00:48:51,887 --> 00:48:55,015
Resistance is futile Jaguar.
You know that.

672
00:48:55,682 --> 00:48:59,603
Or should I just kill you
together with Camia and Lily?

673
00:48:59,686 --> 00:49:04,024
[tense music playing]

674
00:49:20,207 --> 00:49:21,375
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

675
00:49:21,458 --> 00:49:23,126
-[grunts]
-[Damian] <i>Take him.</i>

676
00:49:24,044 --> 00:49:26,380
-[woman] <i>Jaguar! Finish him!</i>
-[gunshots]

677
00:49:29,174 --> 00:49:29,966
[Diego] <i>Dad?</i>

678
00:49:30,050 --> 00:49:32,928
[Helena] <i>Don't worry about</i>
<i>the existence of Lily Cruz.</i>

679
00:49:33,011 --> 00:49:34,763
<i>We'll take our time.</i>

680
00:49:37,641 --> 00:49:41,603
[Lily] <i>Mercedes Palacio</i>
<i>and Helena Montoya.</i>

681
00:49:42,104 --> 00:49:44,523
<i>Hello? Mercedes, can you hear me?</i>

682
00:49:44,606 --> 00:49:46,358
[Lily] <i>I can hear you loud and clear.</i>

683
00:49:46,441 --> 00:49:51,571
<i>You, Helena Montoya,</i>
<i>are none other than Red Dragon.</i>

684
00:49:52,614 --> 00:49:55,909
[theme music playing]
